  "notes": "An everyday transitive verb for moving something slightly out of place or adjusting timing. Very common in both physical and scheduling contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {時間|じかん}をずらす: to shift the time\n- {予定|よてい}をずらす: to reschedule\n- {位置|いち}をずらす: to shift the position\n- {視線|しせん}をずらす: to avert one's gaze\n- {論点|ろんてん}をずらす: to shift the point of argument\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive. The intransitive counterpart is ずれる (to slip, to be off, to be shifted).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {動|うご}かす: to move (more general, can involve larger movements)\n- ずれる: to slip, to be off (intransitive counterpart)\n- {移|うつ}す: to move, to transfer (implies moving to a new location entirely)",
